      "message": "This is exactly the kind of boilerplate that a class hierarchy is supposed to get rid of, yet we now pay the cost of the classes plus the cost of that kind of stuff.\n\n\nIf there is a class hierarchy please consider using *virtual dispatch* on the opaque objects instead of manually inspecting types.\n\n\nclass NetworkSpecifier {\n  public boolean matchesUid(int uid) { return true; /* by default do not check uid. */ }\n}\n\nclass WifiAwareNetworkSpecifier extends NetworkSpecifier {\n  public final int myUid;\n  @Override public boolean matchesUid(int uid) { return uid \u003d\u003d myUid; }\n}\n\nThen this call site becomes (minus the null guard):\n\nif (!networkCapabilities.getNetworkSpecifier().matchesUid(Binder.getCallingUid()) { throw new SecurityException(); }\n\n(if we have a NullSpecifier like suggested in the base patch, we don\u0027t even need a null guard).",
